        "original_id": "cfbd915e-00a1-5948-933b-37a8bfdda806",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Angela Down, Sylvia Pankhurst, Leo Tolstoy, Ian Holm\n- Organizations: BBC\n- Products: War and Peace, Shoulder to Shoulder, We, the Accused\n- Roles: Princess Maria, Myra Bawne\n- Concepts: suffragette movement, left communism, anti-fascism\n\nFacts:\n- Sylvia Pankhurst was born on 5 May 1882 and died on 27 September 1960.\n- Sylvia Pankhurst was an English campaigner in the suffragette movement, a prominent left communist, and later an anti-fascist activist.\n- In 1972, Angela Down played Princess Maria in the 15-hour BBC adaptation of Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace.\n- In 1974, Angela Down starred as Sylvia Pankhurst in the BBC production Shoulder to Shoulder.\n- In 1980, Angela Down played teacher Myra Bawne in the BBC drama serial We, the Accused opposite Ian Holm.",
